    "preamble": "Meat Vyapari Sangharsh Samiti And ... vs State Of Up And 4 Others on 19 November, 2024 Author: Vipin Chandra Dixit Bench: Vipin Chandra Dixit High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc:180779-Db Court No. - 40 Case :- Writ - C No. - 21705 of 2024 Petitioner :- Meat Vyapari Sangharsh Samiti And Another Respondent :- State Of Up And 4 Others Counsel for Petitioner :- Kriti Gupta,Rohan Gupta Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C.,Sant Ram Sharma Hon'ble Shekhar B. Saraf,J. Hon'ble Vipin Chandra Dixit,J.",
    "facts": "iv) Award the cost of the writ petition to the petitioner.\"",
    "arguments": "3. Sri Rohan Gupta, learned counsel appearing on behalf of petitioners submits that insistence of respondent authorities to obtain a NOC from the concerned municipality as a pre-condition for grant/renewal of food license is not necessary as the members of association of the petitioner are merely petty food business operators which are not covered by the Food Safety and Standards (Licensing and Registration of Food Businesses) Regulation, 2011. He further submits that as per Food Safety and Standards (Licensing and Registration of Food Businesses) Regulation, 2011, the petitioners are not required to take any N.O.C. from the Municipal Corporation. He further submits that the stand of the Air Force Authority is that if the proper adequate arrangement is made, these petty shops can operate in the particular area. 4. Learned counsel appearing on behalf of the respondents has vehemently opposed the submissions made by learned counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioners. However, he has fairly submitted that this issue may be re-visited by the officer concerned after granting opportunity of hearing to the petitioners."
  },
